    {
      "text": "Sanofi-Aventis U.S. LLC posted a discontinuation of enoxaparin sodium injection for the U.S. market on 2026-10-20, stating the decision is not related to product safety or quality concerns.",
      "cites": ["E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 87 syringes of the 60 mg/0.6 mL presentation with 10.9 days on hand at 8 per day, and 246 syringes of the 100 mg/mL 0.8 mL presentation with 24.5 days on hand at 10 per day.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General holds 152 syringes of the 100 mg/mL 0.8 mL presentation with 14.5 days on hand at 10.5 per day.",
      "cites": ["D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A label for enoxaparin sodium names Nanjing King-Friend Biochemical Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd. (FEI 3010625707) as a registered plant for analysis, manufacture, and pack, last inspected with a VAI classification on 2023-11-10.",
      "cites": ["E7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection records for that plant show VAI classifications on 2015-05-12, 2018-04-03, and 2023-11-10.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E5", "E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to buy from Amphastar Pharmaceuticals, Inc., which is not on FDA's shortage list today, though its label names no plant we could place.",
